id: pm-jev-pre-create-guard
title: Screen proposed items through a typed pre-create duplicate guard
description: "Give SDK and extension callers a bounded, compact decision before filing tracker work."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-11-18T14:08:58.405Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-18T18:11:44.276Z"
author: codex-sol
acceptance_criteria: "SDK and command share one read-only guard over a certified tracker read; Bounded local model inference returns actionable duplicate, no-match or explicit abstention with no draft text in receipts; Real SDK fixtures, public tracker measurements, documented limitations and repository gates cover the decision path"
comments[11]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-18T14:09:51.665Z",codex-sol,"Ranked by expected agent value per token, qualitatively. 1. A pre-create SDK guard avoids a subprocess and feeding candidate titles and distributions back to an agent on each create. Existing pre-create CLI and ranking primitives do not supply a typed stop/continue/review result. 2. Work selection could connect orientation and claim, but the host already orders work and eligibility depends on current claims and dependencies. 3. Escalation could price a missed handoff, but triage already emits needs_human and a gate accepts custom questions. Backlog triage already streams. The 63-item public baseline has 12 open items and no open item delivering the guard."
  "2026-11-18T14:11:53.338Z",codex-sol,"Design: expose a read-only SDK call and jev guard-create. Use the certified full tracker read and existing title retriever, typed choice request, model admission and optional digest-bound calibration. Retain one overflow candidate so a negative decision on a truncated list abstains. Apply a conservative probability floor, honor stricter settings and disabled fitted policies, and return compact counters and token usage. Fail closed on invalid input or incomplete tracker reads. An unavailable decision endpoint yields a typed abstention."
  "2026-11-18T14:22:18.949Z",codex-sol,"Public tracker measurement at 195fe22, 63 items, limit 3, real local tev1:4b digest 7954dce22bc6. Exact prior title recommended pm-jev-undefined-choice-admission with raw score 0.971799, 519 input tokens, 43.376 s. The SDK receipt used 134 Tev1 tokens versus 430 for the minified detailed JSON. A high none score on a truncated list abstained; zero title candidates reported zero inference tokens. Installed tarball command returned the same duplicate and exited 1. The three new regression tests also passed through pm test."
  "2026-11-18T14:28:30.269Z",codex-sol,"Implementation commit f71c373 includes the SDK, extension, measured public examples, tracker and built distribution. In a packed host a duplicate and an offline abstention both exited 1; an empty shortlist exited 0. A real installed Ollama server with a missing model also abstained. Typecheck, lint, documentation, public provenance, release identity and zero-duplication checks passed. Full coverage and ancillary acceptance are running."
  "2026-11-18T14:30:34.850Z",codex-sol,"A real packed install on the unchanged base reproduced a Bun inference failure. Both Bun 1.3.5 and 1.4.4 mark a native fetch body consumed after the pinned TypeSafe SDK drains its clone while holding and releasing the original reader. This also makes a live guard abstain on a healthy model. Normalize the Bun response stream at the SDK transport boundary and keep deadlines, redirect refusal and native Node behavior."
  "2026-11-18T14:35:07.828Z",codex-sol,"Both native Bun 1.3.5 and 1.4.4 now return the expected duplicate against the real public tracker. A native Response test verifies clone/read behavior and status, headers and URL. Updated two ancillary packed acceptance fixtures that target this entrypoint: use the declared host pin and digest-addressed model for link, and calculate omitted options from the pinned registry for compact triage."
  "2026-11-18T14:39:33.048Z",codex-sol,"After the transport repair, the real guard recommended the same existing item on Node and native Bun 1.3.5 and 1.4.4. The corrected packed install and link acceptance runs pass. The standalone policy module measured 100 percent lines, branches and functions. The earlier full run crossed active source edits, so its coverage percentages are superseded by a fresh run on the final source."
  "2026-11-18T14:43:42.429Z",codex-sol,Commit 44ee76d carries the Bun transport and packed fixture repairs. A full gate caught a CLI help regression in the shared title flag. Restored the detailed dedupe command's optional-title and pair-scan guidance while maintaining the guard's own help. All ten agent-output and pre-create regression tests pass.
  "2026-11-18T14:53:16.634Z",codex-sol,"Code head 934cd0f: npm run coverage passed on Node 26.13.0. All 458 tests passed, none failed, canceled or skipped. All 50 source files were inventoried; c8 covered 8179/8179 statements and lines, 409/409 functions and 3939/3939 branches. A clean build matched every committed dist byte. The final packed SDK and installed guard returned the public duplicate in Node and Bun with the expected CLI exit code."
  "2026-11-18T14:57:19.425Z",codex-sol,"Final gates: npm run typecheck, lint, duplication, docstring, verify:public-provenance and verify:release-identity passed. git fetch --tags origin followed by npm run changelog:full and npm run changelog:check passed. The four acceptance test files passed together, 5/5 and no skips, via node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-reporter=tap test/install.acceptance.ts test/joint-install.acceptance.ts test/link.acceptance.ts test/live.acceptance.ts. All eleven standalone public/synthetic evidence generators also ran, including a 12-pair quality run and a 69-pair historical calibration run on verified public snapshots with actual labels in both splits. All generated benchmark artifacts stayed in scratch. pm test --run --progress passed the four guard regressions. Strict tracker health passed in an isolated checkout. Releasing the claim for verification."
  "2026-11-18T18:11:42.885Z",codex-sol,"Round CN verified six CodeRabbit findings against d0968ee. Commit 309f8ee includes each fix and a regression.\nPRRT_kwDOU8IMzs65Dbxm -> 309f8ee resolves the nested tracker before policy and calibration reads.\nPRRT_kwDOU8IMzs65DbxD -> 309f8ee binds calibration to the admitted digest and abstains when the tag moves during admission.\nPRRT_kwDOU8IMzs65DbyN -> 309f8ee retains only validated input and output token counts in usage.\nPRRT_kwDOU8IMzs65DbyA -> 309f8ee rejects an explicitly empty limit through the packed CLI.\nPRRT_kwDOU8IMzs65Dbxz -> 309f8ee consumes the complete list after one host certification.\nPRRT_kwDOU8IMzs65Dbyx -> 309f8ee verifies three retained options and the case where the selected label is retained as a fourth.\nTypecheck, build:test, lint, duplication, docstrings, public provenance and release identity passed. The focused guard and calibration run passed 15/15. npm run coverage passed 462/462 with zero skips across 50 source files. c8 measured 8182/8182 statements and lines, 3945/3945 branches and 409/409 functions. Tag fetch, full changelog regeneration and changelog:check passed.\nAll four Node acceptance files passed, totaling 5 tests. Joint install timed out on the first Node 24 run and passed unchanged on Node 26. All eleven standalone acceptance files passed using verified public snapshots or synthetic fixtures, including the six-repository duplicate-quality and dedupe-calibration samples with 15 and 96 model calls respectively. Reports stayed in scratch storage."
